
# Windows Server 2019 Installation

## Overview

This document covers the installation of Windows Server 2019 in an Oracle VirtualBox virtual machine.

The purpose of this setup was to create a virtual server environment for learning Windows Server administration and eventually working with Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS).

## Technologies Used

- Windows Server 2019
- Oracle VirtualBox
- Virtual Machine (VM)
- Windows Server installation ISO

## Installation Process

### 1. Virtual Machine Setup

Created a new virtual machine in Oracle VirtualBox to host Windows Server 2019.

Configured the virtual machine with the necessary system resources and attached the Windows Server 2019 installation ISO.

### 2. Windows Server Installation

Booted the virtual machine using the Windows Server 2019 installation ISO.

Followed the Windows Setup process to install the operating system.

### 3. Initial Server Configuration

After installation, accessed the Windows Server desktop and opened Server Manager.

Server Manager provides a centralized interface for managing server roles, features, and system settings.

### 4. Server Manager

Verified that Windows Server was running successfully and accessed the Server Manager dashboard.

This interface would later be used to manage server roles and configure additional services.

